{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rbkhgsy6cvkpybhu436r5c7jsy4f7lct4uyt5jd6yf65lu4r5sja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases passed.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/src/lib.c` — 164 lines, 5 exported functions (`create_block`, `allocate_block`, `free_block`, `compute_hash`, `betagamma`). One build configuration: CMake compiles a single TU with no `-D` defines, and the C source has zero `#ifdef`s → the Rust crate correspondingly has one (empty) feature set.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 5 C `nm -D` symbols, all present in the Rust `.so`; import-side table; **0 missing** |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 18 rows, one per distinct rejection grepped from the C (`return NULL` ×2, `return -1`, both `free_block` guards, both unchecked derefs, unbounded `strcpy`, boundary constants, narrow-parameter/enum FFI cases) |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 46 rows = pruned cross-product of the axes the C actually branches on (name lengths 0/1/31/32-35, signed-`char` bytes, all 256 `flags`, `count` 0/1/2-14/4096/overflow, all 19 `param1 % 10` residues, all 5 truncation-sign classes of `(sum1-sum2)/10`, all 7 reachable `compute_hash` pointer orderings, 4 overflow classes) |\n\n## Two non-obvious blockers I had to solve\n1. **`betagamma` is not a function of its arguments.** It calls `compute_hash`, which compares raw `malloc`/`calloc` *addresses*. The C library itself returns 517/527/617/627 for `betagamma(1,2,3,4)` depending on tcache state. Fixed by running each implementation in a child `fork()`ed from the *same* parent heap image (harness allocates nothing between the two forks), so both observe byte-identical allocator state.\n2. **C leaves indeterminate bytes.** `create_block` returns an uninitialised `DataBlock` with only `strlen+1` bytes written, so `name[strlen+1..]` is stack garbage in C (verified empirically). Only the defined region is compared.\n\n## Phases B/C — two real divergences found and fixed in `src/lib.rs`\nBoth on error paths, both invisible to happy-path tests:\n- `compute_hash(NULL, p)`: C → **SIGSEGV(11)**, Rust → **SIGABRT(6)** (`\"null pointer dereference occurred\"`). rustc instruments `(*mb1).data` with a null check. Fixed with an uninstrumented load (`load_data_field` via libc `memcpy` + `offset_of!`).\n- `create_block(id, NULL, flags)`: same class of bug in the hand-written copy loop. Fixed by calling libc `strcpy` — which is what the C does (it imports `strcpy@GLIBC_2.2.5`), so the Rust `.so` now imports the identical symbol.\n\n## Phase D — gate\n`scripts/verify_all.sh`: 2 feature combos × 2 profiles (dev **and** release, since optimisation level changes whether the UB instrumentation exists — a real behavioural axis here) → check, build, `nm -D` diff (0 missing), full suite. **All 4 configurations pass.**\n\nNon-vacuity proven three ways: an independent `model_without_hash` oracle that predicts every term of `betagamma` except the 9 possible hash values; `scripts/traceability.sh` confirming all 46+18 rows are referenced by test labels; and **18 injected mutations — 16 caught, 2 survivors proven equivalent** (dropping `if (mb->data)` just yields the no-op `free(NULL)`; a fixed-32-byte copy is unobservable because `temp_name`/`special.name` are never read and post-NUL bytes are indeterminate).\n\n`c_src/` sources were not modified (only the generated `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":176801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1116,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"569f5cd2-f847-493a-93e8-51a8602e3501","uuid":"420cd20d-d189-47ed-869b-e2de58b774b8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:57:24.028Z"}
